  "system": "You are answering simple retrospective perception questions about one observed 2D rollout. Use the 32 ordered observable JSON states only. Do not predict unshown physics, estimate pixel distances, infer a hidden goal, or choose an action. Return one JSON object mapping every question_id to exactly one option letter.",
  "user_text": "The supplied JSON contains 32 uniformly sampled observable states in chronological order. STATE 01 means state_index 0 and STATE 32 means state_index 31. Coordinates use a bottom-left origin: x increases to the right and y increases upward.\nThe orange circle/tool is the placed tool and the red circle/ball is the target ball.\nThis is a qualitative retrospective reading test. Answer only what is clearly visible in the supplied states; no goal, gravity label, or success/failure label is supplied.\n\nFalling_2_downward:tool_vertical_direction_v3: When the orange tool visibly moves away from its starting position, does it move upward or downward?\n  A. upward\n  B. downward\nFalling_2_downward:red_endpoint_horizontal_v3: Compared with where it started, does the red ball finish clearly to the left or clearly to the right?\n  A. right\n  B. left"
